#: ../../integration_guides/ITSM/ServiceNow.rst:33
msgid "CREDENTIALS"
msgstr "CREDENTIALS"

#: ../../integration_guides/ITSM/ServiceNow.rst:32
msgid ""
"Supply credentials for a user in ServiceNow that is able to access the REST "
"interface and create/update/delete incidents, requests, requested items, "
"item options, catalog items, workflows, etc. The list of necessary roles "
"includes ``x_moda_morpheus_ca.integration`` (available if the |morpheus| "
"ServiceNow plugin is installed from the ServiceNow Store), "
"``catalog_admin``, ``itil``, ``rest_service``, ``web_service_admin`` and "
"``import_transformer``."
msgstr ""
"Supply credentials para un usuario in ServiceNow que es capaz de acceso el "
"REST interfaz y create/update/delete incidents, requests, requested "
"elementos, elemento opciones, catalog elementos, workflows, etc. The lista "
"of necesario roles includes ``x_moda_morpheus_ca.integration`` (disponible "
"if el |morpheus| ServiceNow plugin es instalado desde el ServiceNow Store), "
"``catalog_admin``, ``itil``, ``rest_service``, ``web_service_admin`` y "
"``import_transformer``."

#: ../../integration_guides/ITSM/ServiceNow.rst:34
msgid ""
"|morpheus| supports simple and OAuth 2.0 authentication with ServiceNow. See"
" the next section for additional details on configuring the ServiceNow "
"appliance for OAuth 2.0 authentication if you intend to use it. When "
"supplying credentials to |morpheus| users may opt to integrate with a saved "
"set of username and password credentials, a saved set of OAuth 2.0 "
"credentials, a new set of username and password credentials (not saved), or "
"a new set of credentials (OAuth 2.0 or username/password) which will also be"
" saved to the |morpheus| credential store for later use. Once the credential"
" type is selected, the fields in the modal will adjust to correspond to the "
"chosen credential type. Once again, see the next section for more details on"
" configuring OAuth 2.0 authentication."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| supports simple y OAuth 2.0 authentication con ServiceNow. See el"
" siguiente sección para adicional detalles on configuring el ServiceNow "
"appliance para OAuth 2.0 authentication if you intend to use it. When "
"supplying credentials to |morpheus| users puede opt to integrate con un "
"saved set of nombre de usuario y contraseña credentials, un saved set of "
"OAuth 2.0 credentials, un nuevo set of nombre de usuario y contraseña "
"credentials (no saved), o un nuevo set of credentials (OAuth 2.0 o nombre de"
" usuario/contraseña) cual será también be saved to el |morpheus| credential "
"store para later use. Once el credential tipo es seleccionado, el campos in "
"el modal será adjust to correspond to el chosen credential tipo. Once again,"
" see el siguiente sección para más detalles on configuring OAuth 2.0 "
"authentication."

